  "body": "Follow-up to #128. The MCP server is headless (no GPU), so an agent cannot see the stock simulation or a viewport.\n\nWanted: a tool that returns a render of the simulated stock, or of the toolpath over the model, as an MCP image content block. Prefer a CPU path (an offscreen software rasteriser over the stock_sim mesh) so CI stays GPU-free. Also a numeric summary: rest material volume and its bounds.\n\nDone means: a tool returns a PNG of the stock after generation, deterministically, in a headless test.\n",
